  "source_notes": "Compiled for the 2025-26 NCAA Division I academic year (current as of June 2026; the 2026-27 Pac-12 rebuild and the related Mountain West/WAC/ASUN moves had NOT yet taken effect, so they are NOT reflected here). Per task spec, ALL full member institutions of every D1 conference are listed regardless of whether the school actually sponsors tennis; men's and women's files are identical full memberships. Sources: Wikipedia 'List of NCAA Division I institutions', 'List of NCAA conferences', and individual conference pages (en.wikipedia.org); NCAA.com; conference official sites (theamerican.org, conferenceusa.com, themw.com, asunsports.org, wacsports.com, southland.org, mvc-sports.com, ovcsports.com, bigsouthsports.com, necsports.com, meacsports.com). Notable points: (1) Pac-12 shows its 2025-26 state with only Oregon State and Washington State as full members. (2) Mountain West still includes Boise State, Colorado State, Fresno State, San Diego State, Utah State (they depart for the Pac-12 on 2026-07-01) plus new member Grand Canyon. (3) The American Conference is listed by its 13 FULL members; Army and Navy are football-only affiliates and are excluded. (4) WAC, ASUN, Big South, MVC, Southland, OVC, NEC reflect 2025-26 rosters before the July 2026 UAC/Big Sky/Big West reshuffle. (5) Saint Francis (PA) is still D1 for 2025-26. (6) Oregon State and Washington State are listed under the Pac-12 (their actual membership); in 2025-26 they place most sports in the WCC under a temporary scheduling alliance but are NOT full WCC members, so they are not double-counted there. (7) Hartford and a few others have left D1 and are excluded. autobid=true for all conferences (every listed conference crowns a champion that earns an NCAA automatic bid).",
